---
import Alert from "../components/ui/Alert.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/ui/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/ui/PageHeader.astro";
import { pageTitle, site } from "../config/site";
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
---

<Page
  title={pageTitle("Privacy")}
  description="What NetworksInsights does with your data today: no accounts, no cookies, no analytics, and one theme preference stored on your device."
>
  <div class="grid gap-4">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Privacy" }]} />
    <PageHeader
      title="Privacy"
      intro={`This page describes what ${site.name} does with your data today. It is short because the site does very little.`}
    >
      <Alert tone="warning" title="Draft: owner input needed">
        This page is a draft and has not been reviewed. Before launch the owner must provide the
        name of the party responsible for the site, a contact email and the legal jurisdiction, and
        confirm the hosting paragraph. All of this is listed in the launch checklist.
      </Alert>
    </PageHeader>
  </div>

  <div class="ni-prose">
    <h2>In short</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>There are no accounts and no sign-up.</li>
      <li>The site sets no cookies.</li>
      <li>The site has no analytics and no advertising trackers today.</li>
      <li>Your theme choice is stored on your own device and never sent to us.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What the site does</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name}{" "}
      is a set of static pages. Loading a page does not ask you for information, and the site has no
      forms that send data to us. The fonts are served from the site itself, so your browser does
      not contact a font service either.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
      The site sets no cookies. It stores one item in your browser's local storage, under the key
      <code>ni-theme</code>: your choice of light, dark or system theme, if you make one. It stays
      on your device, and the site does not read it for any other purpose.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      There are no analytics today. If that changes, this page will be updated before analytics go
      live.
    </p>

    <h2>Tools and your files</h2>
    <p>
      No tools are live yet, so no files are processed today. Where a tool runs in your browser,
      your files stay on your device. This page will say where each tool does its processing once
      tools launch.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on Cloudflare. To deliver a page, Cloudflare necessarily receives technical
      request data, such as your IP address and the page you asked for. See
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>
      for how it handles that data.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>[The name of the responsible party and a contact email: to be provided.]</p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>[The legal jurisdiction: to be provided.]</p>
  </div>
</Page>
